"""The standing lay of a charged record in the well of the holder of the sign (the cold reader's verdicts of 2026-10-19, "the fixed point stands" and "the levels, what stands", their sections 0 the recipes, and the design verdict of the same day, section 7, the generic form by the owner's word; ALGEBRA.md, The atom is a bound body of the holder of the sign; At a Node there is Rule3 and nothing else): the mode file of a world whose record of a plane family reads the holder of the sign under its act `rotation`, laid as an eigenvector of the well the holder already writes, in the engine's own phase convention, so that the record stands on the engine; the generator carries no law but Rule3's own lines and the files' declarations, and names no family, no world and no number of the law. The source bodies (`--source`, a family of one-Node bodies) are laid as the generator's one-Node pixel record of their count in the sense `--sense` (2 A^2 sin omega_s = T per quantum at the pair's own omega_s: A = isqrt(count T den / (2 den sin omega_s)) by the engine's search and division acts, the level before at the pair's rest rotation in the body's sense, (A cos omega_s, sense A sin omega_s), tools/pixel_mode.py's `pixel_record` mirrored by name; at the frozen pair num = 0 the amplitude is isqrt(T / 2) and im_before sense x A); the standing record (`--record`) is laid in four steps. (1) The well: the world is loaded once with the record's levels all 0, so that the engine's own start writes the holder's rows under the sources alone, and the row the record reads is read off the lattice (every row of the holder but the record's own, `loader/derived.row_of`), h_i, the well U_i = -k_r h_i / Gamma with k_r the weight the record reads the holder with (the engine's turn: each Link's pair turns by 1 / Gamma per unit of the holder's level difference across it per interval; the centre rotates faster by k_r |h| / Gamma, so the well is positive at the centre). (2) The eigenproblem in doubles: Rule3's own standing line at every Node from the engine's rule integers of the record's read at the start (`node.rule_of` on the engine's own read, `Lattice.read`: the six reaches R_ij, the own weight S_i and the wall w at the Node's content and the Links' factors; `rule_arrays`), 2 cos(Omega + U_i) phi_i = SUM_j (R_ij / w) phi_j + (S_i / w) phi_i, in the law's weighted form where the paces differ (ALGEBRA.md #the-paces, The clock is the Node's, the tension is the Link's: D M is symmetric at every pace with D = diag(1 / p_i^2)), so the symmetric operator is B chi = 2 cos Omega chi with B_ij = (R_ij / w) (p_j / p_i) / sqrt(cos U_i cos U_j) on the Links whose far Node stands on the board (0 beyond an open or closed face, the fill; the wrap on a periodic axis; the Node's own level on an axis of one layer, its reach back on the diagonal) and B_ii = S_i / w + 2 sin Omega sin U_i / cos U_i, and phi_i = p_i chi_i / sqrt(cos U_i) (`operator`); where the record reads no holder of the content the paces are the vacuum's, R_ij / w = num / (3 den) on every Link and S_i = 0, the special case the recipes wrote; its top eight eigenvectors from one fixed start vector and one tolerance (`START_SEED`, `TOLERANCE`), the solver asked for more pairs than the eight kept (`SOLVED`, so that its cut falls beyond them: a cut inside a degenerate cluster misconverges the pairs at the cut), so that the lay and the mode file's digest are the same on every run; the level named by `--level` (1s, 2s or 2p: the kinds by the monopole and the dipole, s, s, p, p, p, d, d, d; the 2p the degenerate triplet's combination with the largest dipole along x, the 2p_x) and Omega iterated in sin Omega to the level's own fixed point (the potential term moves an excited level where the ground's sin Omega is used for it); phi normalised to 1 at its largest, the sign positive at the centre for an s level and along +x for the 2p_x. (3) The amplitude, one quantum: A = sqrt(T / (2 SUM phi_i^2 sin(Omega + U_i))), so that the lay's Wronskian SUM A^2 phi_i^2 sin(Omega + U_i), the angle from the level before to the level now at the Node i, is T / 2, the charge of one quantum and the count on the board (the cold reader's ruling of 2026-10-22; until then A = sqrt(T / (2 sin omega_0 SUM phi^2)) at the free rotation omega_0 = arccos(num / den), whose Wronskian in the well read 1.17 to 1.24 T / 2, history). (4) The lay in the engine's phase convention (the second verdict's test, exact at the first steps: lattice.step applies the phase act before Rule3, so the gauge-flat solution is z_i(t) = phi_i e^(-i U_i) e^(-i (Omega + U_i) t), the NOW level carrying the well's angle -U_i per Node and the level before the one angle Omega): now_i = rint(A phi_i cos U_i), im_now_i = rint(-A phi_i sin U_i), before_i = rint(A phi_i cos Omega), im_before_i = rint(A phi_i sin Omega); the rounding at most half a level per Node, one interval of the walk's size (the first verdict's lay, now = A phi and before at Omega + U_i, differs by the Node-dependent factor e^(-i U_i) and jumps at the deep Node on the first step, then stands breathing). With `--level a+b` (several levels joined by '+', e.g. `1s+2p`) the lay is the sum of the named levels' lays, each level at its own Omega in the before term and the common well's angle on the now term, each at 1 / n of the quantum, A_k = sqrt(T / (2 n SUM phi_k^2 sin(Omega_k + U_i))), the four arrays summed before the rounding (the step is linear, so the sum of standing solutions is a solution; the design verdict of 2026-10-19, section 5, the line), the readings naming the levels, their Omegas and the beats between them; with `--shares s_1,s_2,...` (integers from 1, one per named level) the levels at their shares of the quantum, A_k = sqrt(s_k T / (2 S SUM phi_k^2 sin(Omega_k + U_i))) with S their sum, the equal lay where none are given (2026-10-22, the pure level's worlds: a body at the shares (0.9, 0.1) of its two levels). With `--seed n` (from 1) the lay's rounding seed: every level dithered within half a unit by a seeded uniform draw before its rounding, so the lay differs from the plain rounding by at most one unit per Node, within the lay's own grain, the same well and the same levels to the rounding and another sequence of the click's read of the board; 0, the plain rounding (2026-10-22, the geometric law of the pure level's first click measured over the rounding seeds). With `--lay gaussian` the record is laid instead as the free lump the builder's probe laid, the control that does not stand: a Gaussian of width `--sigma` Nodes at the free rotation, now = rint(scale x g) with scale^2 = T den / (2 s SUM g^2), before = now num div den and im_before = now s div den with s = isqrt(den^2 - num^2), the floor divisions of that lay. The mode file is written beside the world with the world's digest, the sources' entries and the record's; beside it `<world>.standing.json` keeps the tool's own readings (the well along an axis, the rule's integers over the wall, the level, Omega, omega_0, the binding, A, the peak level, the lay's radial profile, the Wronskian, the eight levels' Omega and kinds), labelled a lattice reading and no number of the blind. The world's declared counts (one Node, one count per body) are the gate's; the record's share at every Node is below a quantum, so its declared Node and count stand as the gate admits them within its rounding (ENGINE.md section 6, step 2). Every integer is the files' and the engine's; the tool holds no number of the law but the recipes' steps, and the recipes' own numbers (the radii of the profile, the levels and the iterations of the eigensolver, its start seed and tolerance, the kinds' threshold, the fixed point's first Omega below the free rotation, the lump's width) stand in `tools/standing_lay.json` beside this file and not in the code, since the tools' gate admits no literal beyond the law's own integers in a tool that touches the engine (tests/test_rule3.py).

Run with PYTHONPATH set to the checkout's src:

    PYTHONPATH=src python tools/standing_lay.py --input <world>.json --record <family> --source <family> --sense -1 [--lay standing --level 1s | --lay standing --level 1s+2p | --lay gaussian --sigma 4]
 The centred count (2026-10-23, the owner's decision; ALGEBRA.md, The turn per proper interval; node.phased, node.phase_counts): the engine's Link phase at the step centred at the interval m is K(m + 1) theta_0 / 2 with K(m + 1) = 2 (Phi(m + 1) - Phi(m)) - c = (2 m + 1) c for a static potential, so the standing solution's frame is z_i(m) = e^(i u_i (m + 1/2)) y_i(m), u_i the Node's angle per interval, and the lay at the interval 0 carries half the Node's angle on now and minus half on before, now = A phi e^(-i U / 2) and before = A phi e^(i (Omega + U / 2)) with U = -u in this module's sign; the standing operator and the Wronskian A^2 phi^2 sin(Omega + U) are the former's, the frame's offset alone moved from one interval to half (to that day the left sum N(m + 1) = (m + 1) c, the frame e^(i u (m + 1)), now = A phi e^(-i U) and before = A phi e^(i Omega))."""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import json
from pathlib import Path
from typing import Any

import numpy as np
import scipy.sparse as sp  # type: ignore[import-untyped]
from scipy.sparse.linalg import eigsh  # type: ignore[import-untyped]

from event_universe import node, world_files
from event_universe.core import paces
from event_universe.core.ports import PORT_SIDES
from event_universe.core.rule3 import division_forward, largest_below
from event_universe.lattice import Lattice
from event_universe.loader.derived import FamilyRule, row_of
from event_universe.loader.universe import universe_of
from event_universe.world_files import input_digest, load_world

LABEL = "lattice reading"
RECIPE = json.loads(
    Path(__file__).with_suffix(".json").read_text(encoding="utf-8")
)  # the recipe's own numbers, a file's keys beside the tool and no number in the code (tests/test_rule3.py, the tools' gate)
RADII = tuple(int(r) for r in RECIPE["radii"])  # the radii the profile is read within, the verdicts'
ITERATIONS = int(
    RECIPE["iterations"]
)  # the fixed point of Omega is reached in five; the bound is a guard
LEVELS = int(RECIPE["levels"])  # the top eigenvectors kept: s, s, p, p, p, d, d, d
SOLVED = int(
    RECIPE["solved"]
)  # the eigenpairs asked of the solver, more than the levels kept, so that the solver's cut falls beyond them
KINDS = {
    "1s": ("s", 0),
    "2s": ("s", 1),
    "2p": ("p", 0),
}  # a level by its kind and its rank among that kind
START_SEED = int(
    RECIPE["start_seed"]
)  # the eigensolver's one start vector, seeded here and nowhere else
TOLERANCE = float(
    RECIPE["tolerance"]
)  # the eigensolver's relative tolerance and the fixed point's, named with the start
THRESHOLD = float(
    RECIPE["kind_threshold"]
)  # an eigenvector's monopole or dipole over its size, below it 0
START_BELOW = float(
    RECIPE["start_below_omega_0"]
)  # the fixed point's first Omega, below the free rotation
SIGMA = float(RECIPE["sigma"])  # the free lump's width in Nodes, --lay gaussian


def family_index(families: tuple[FamilyRule, ...], name: str) -> int:
    """A family's index by its name; refused by name otherwise."""
    for index, family in enumerate(families):
        if family.name == name:
            return index
    raise ValueError(f"no family {name!r} in the universe: {[f.name for f in families]}")


def read_of(family: FamilyRule, families: tuple[FamilyRule, ...]) -> tuple[int, int]:
    """The holder of the sign the family reads and the weight k_r it reads with; refused where it reads none."""
    for read in family.reads:
        if families[read.family].wronskian:
            return read.family, read.weight
    raise ValueError(f"{family.name!r} reads no holder of the sign: no well to stand in")


def pixel_entry(
    family: FamilyRule,
    node_at: tuple[int, int, int],
    shape: tuple[int, ...],
    action: int,
    sense: int,
    count: int,
) -> dict[str, Any]:
    """A one-Node record of `count` quanta of a plane family at its pair, the generator's one-Node declaration by name (tools/pixel_mode.py, `pixel_record`, mirrored with the engine's own acts; ALGEBRA.md, The law's alpha is a coefficient of the file, the quantum of a family: 2 A^2 sin omega_s = T per quantum, its Wronskian sense x T / 2 per quantum): the level now (A, 0) with A the largest integer whose square is at most count T den div (2 den sin omega_s), den sin omega_s the largest integer whose square is at most den^2 - num^2, and the level before the pair's rest rotation in the body's sense, (A num div den, sense x A den sin omega_s div den); at the frozen pair num = 0 the amplitude isqrt(T / 2) and im_before sense x A; a family of other than one plane per part refused by name (the generator lays several planes alike, the one-Node entry here is one plane's)."""
    if family.planes != 1:
        raise ValueError(
            f"{family.name!r} is laid as a one-Node source and has {family.planes} planes per part: the one-Node entry "
            "here is one plane's"
        )
    num, den = family.pair
    sine = paces.sine_den(num, den)
    amplitude = largest_below(int(division_forward(count * action * den, 2 * sine, 0)[0]))
    before = int(division_forward(amplitude * num, den, 0)[0])
    im_before = sense * int(division_forward(amplitude * sine, den, 0)[0])
    size = int(np.prod(shape))
    flat = (node_at[0] * shape[1] + node_at[1]) * shape[2] + node_at[2]
    zeros = [0] * size
    moving = {key: zeros.copy() for key in ("now", "before", "im_now", "im_before")}
    moving["now"][flat], moving["before"][flat], moving["im_before"][flat] = amplitude, before, im_before
    return {
        "family": family.name,
        "pair": list(family.pair),
        "amplitude": amplitude,
        "count": count,
        "moving": moving,
    }


def levels_entry(family: FamilyRule, lay: dict[str, np.ndarray]) -> dict[str, Any]:
    """A record's mode entry from its four level arrays over the lattice, x-major, one integer per Node."""
    return {
        "family": family.name,
        "pair": list(family.pair),
        "amplitude": int(np.abs(lay["now"]).max()),
        "count": 1,
        "moving": {
            key: [int(v) for v in np.asarray(lay[key]).ravel()]
            for key in ("now", "before", "im_now", "im_before")
        },
    }


def zero_lay(shape: tuple[int, ...]) -> dict[str, np.ndarray]:
    """The record's levels all 0, the lay of the well's reading pass."""
    return {key: np.zeros(shape, dtype=np.int64) for key in ("now", "before", "im_now", "im_before")}


def mode_document(
    world: dict[str, Any], entries: list[dict[str, Any]], packets: list[dict[str, Any]] | None = None
) -> dict[str, Any]:
    """The mode file: the world's digest and one entry per body in the world's order."""
    return {"world_digest": input_digest(world), "bodies": entries, "packets": list(packets or [])}


def entries_of(
    world: dict[str, Any],
    families: tuple[FamilyRule, ...],
    record: str,
    source: str,
    sense: int,
    lay: dict[str, np.ndarray],
) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:
    """The bodies' entries in the world's order: the sources as one-Node pixel records of their declared count (one Node each, refused by name otherwise), the record from `lay`; a body of another family is refused by name."""
    shape = tuple(int(v) for v in world["shape"])
    found = []
    for number, body in enumerate(world["bodies"]):
        family = families[family_index(families, str(body["family"]))]
        if body["family"] == source:
            if len(body["nodes"]) != 1:
                raise ValueError(
                    f"bodies[{number}] of {source!r} stands at {len(body['nodes'])} Nodes: a source here is laid at one Node"
                )
            node_at = tuple(int(v) for v in body["nodes"][0]["node"])
            count = int(body["nodes"][0].get("count", 1))
            found.append(
                pixel_entry(
                    family,
                    (node_at[0], node_at[1], node_at[2]),
                    shape,
                    int(world_action(world)),
                    sense,
                    count,
                )
            )
        elif body["family"] == record:
            found.append(levels_entry(family, lay))
        else:
            raise ValueError(
                f"bodies[{number}] is of {body['family']!r}, neither the source {source!r} nor the record {record!r}"
            )
    return found


def universe_of_world(world: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:
    """The universe file the world names, read from the repository root."""
    return dict(
        json.loads(
            world_files.REPOSITORY_ROOT.joinpath(str(world["universe"])).read_text(encoding="utf-8")
        )
    )


def world_action(world: dict[str, Any]) -> int:
    """The universe's quantum action T."""
    return int(universe_of_world(world)["integers"]["quantum_action"])


def well_of(path: Path, record: str) -> tuple[np.ndarray, int, int, int, Lattice]:
    """The well the record reads, from the engine's own start with the record's levels at 0: the sum of the holder's rows' time lines but the record's own, h_i; with it the record's family index, the holder's index, k_r and the board at its start, whose read the rule's integers are taken from."""
    world = load_world(path)
    board = Lattice(world, None)
    families = board.families
    index = family_index(families, record)
    holder, weight = read_of(families[index], families)
    own = row_of(families, index, 0)
    width = families[holder].width
    lines = board.states[holder].lines
    rows = len(lines) // width
    h = np.zeros(world.shape, dtype=np.int64)
    for row in range(rows):
        if row == own:
            continue
        h += np.asarray(lines[row * width].now, dtype=np.int64)
    return h, index, holder, weight, board


def well_angles(board: Lattice, index: int, gamma: int) -> np.ndarray:
    """The well's angle per interval at every Node as the engine turns it (the centred count, 2026-10-23): the record's clocked potential c = rounded(L p_0 / Gamma) at the lay (`node.turning`, `node.rulers`, `paces.turn_factor`, the same integers node.phased writes into the phase row), the Node's angle U_i = -2 c_i theta' with theta' = arccos(1 - 1 / (8 Gamma^2)) the half-angle act's angle (features/phase at the unit 2 Gamma; K advances by 2 c per interval), in this module's sign; the former reading, to that day, the float -weight h / Gamma, half a count off the engine's turn at worst."""
    angles = node.turning(index, board.families, board.states, 1, 0)
    assert angles is not None  # a standing lay is read for a turned record alone
    clock = node.rulers(index, board.families, board.states, 1, board.wrap, gamma, 0)[0]
    counts = np.asarray(
        np.broadcast_to(
            np.asarray(paces.turn_factor(angles[0], clock, gamma), dtype=object), board.shape
        ),
        dtype=np.float64,
    )
    half_act = float(np.arccos(1 - 1 / (8 * gamma * gamma)))
    return -2 * counts * half_act


def rule_arrays(board: Lattice, index: int) -> tuple[list[np.ndarray], np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:
    """Rule3's integers at every Node for the record's own read at the start (`Lattice.read`, the content at the Node and its six Links' factors, every sign row but the record's own; `node.rule_of`, core/rule3.rule_integers): the six reaches over the wall, R_ij / w per Port in Port order, the own weight over the wall, S_i / w, and the Node's pace p_i (`paces.node_paces`), each over the lattice in doubles, the integers exact in them; the plain rule at Gamma, R_ij / w = num / (3 den) and S_i = 0, where the record reads no holder of the content."""
    family, gamma = board.families[index], board.world.node_clock
    content, factors = board.read(index)
    rule = node.rule_of(family, gamma, content, factors, board.unit)
    pace = paces.node_paces(gamma, content)[1]
    wall = float(rule.wall)

    def over(value: Any) -> np.ndarray:
        return np.array(np.broadcast_to(np.asarray(value, dtype=np.float64), board.shape))

    return [over(reach) / wall for reach in rule.reaches], over(rule.self_coefficient) / wall, over(pace)


def operator(
    reaches: list[np.ndarray],
    own: np.ndarray,
    pace: np.ndarray,
    well: np.ndarray,
    omega: float,
    periodic: tuple[bool, bool, bool],
) -> sp.csr_matrix:
    """The symmetric operator of Rule3's standing line at the angle Omega (the module's step 2): B_ij = (R_ij / w) (p_j / p_i) / sqrt(cos U_i cos U_j) for each Link through a Port whose far Node stands on the board (the wrap on a periodic axis; nothing beyond an open or closed face, where the Link sends the fill), the Link of an axis of one layer sending the Node's own level and so its reach back on the diagonal, and B_ii = S_i / w + 2 sin Omega sin U_i / cos U_i; symmetric by the law's weight 1 / p_i^2, taken as the mean of the matrix and its transpose, the same matrix where the paces are uniform. The symmetrization by sqrt(cos U_i cos U_j) holds for a well within a quarter turn at every Node (cos U > 0); beyond it no operator is formed, a limit of this symmetrization and not of the standing line, which holds at any U, nor of the law, whose bound is the Node's turn below a half turn per interval (2026-10-20, the reader's word): a deeper well wants the unitary frame."""
    shape = well.shape
    size = int(np.prod(shape))
    index = np.arange(size).reshape(shape)
    flat_well = well.ravel()
    cosines = np.cos(flat_well)
    scale = 1 / cosines ** (1 / 2)
    relative = pace.ravel() / pace.max()
    diagonal = own.ravel() + 2 * float(np.sin(omega)) * np.sin(flat_well) / cosines
    rows, cols, values = [], [], []
    for port, (axis, side) in enumerate(PORT_SIDES):
        reach = reaches[port].ravel()
        if (
            shape[axis] == 1
        ):  # the Link reaches the Node itself: its flux 0, its reach back on the diagonal
            diagonal = diagonal + reach
            continue
        far = np.roll(index, -side, axis=axis)
        inside = np.ones(shape, dtype=bool)
        if not periodic[axis]:
            edge: list[slice] = [slice(None)] * 3
            edge[axis] = slice(-1, None) if side > 0 else slice(0, 1)
            inside[tuple(edge)] = False
        near, there = index[inside].ravel(), far[inside].ravel()
        rows.append(near)
        cols.append(there)
        values.append(reach[near] * (scale[near] * scale[there]) * (relative[there] / relative[near]))
    links = sp.coo_matrix(
        (np.concatenate(values), (np.concatenate(rows), np.concatenate(cols))), shape=(size, size)
    ).tocsr()
    return ((links + links.T) / 2 + sp.diags(diagonal)).tocsr()


def kind_of(phi: np.ndarray, grids: list[np.ndarray]) -> str:
    """An eigenvector's kind by its monopole and its dipole: p where its dipole stands, s where its monopole stands and no dipole, d or other otherwise."""
    size = float(np.abs(phi).sum())
    dipole = max(abs(float((phi * grid).sum())) for grid in grids)
    if dipole > THRESHOLD * size:
        return "p"
    return "s" if abs(float(phi.sum())) > THRESHOLD * size else "d"


def level_index(kinds: list[str], level: str) -> int:
    """The index of the named level among the eigenvectors by their kinds, the first of a p triplet; refused by name where the top eight do not hold it."""
    kind, rank = KINDS[level]
    found = [j for j, k in enumerate(kinds) if k == kind]
    if kind == "p":
        found = [j for j in found if j + 2 < len(kinds) and kinds[j + 1] == kinds[j + 2] == "p"]
    if len(found) <= rank:
        raise ValueError(
            f"the level {level} is not among the top {len(kinds)} eigenvectors (the kinds {kinds})"
        )
    return found[rank]


def eigenvectors(
    reaches: list[np.ndarray],
    own: np.ndarray,
    pace: np.ndarray,
    well: np.ndarray,
    omega_0: float,
    periodic: tuple[bool, bool, bool],
    level: str,
) -> tuple[np.ndarray, float, list[dict[str, Any]]]:
    """The named level of Rule3's standing line and its Omega: the top eigenvectors of the operator (`operator`) sorted by their eigenvalue, the solver asked for `solved` pairs and the top `levels` kept (a cut inside a degenerate cluster misconverges the pairs at the cut, so the cut is kept beyond the levels read: at eight pairs on the cube of 33 the 3d triplet was cut and the 2p misread at one iteration), Omega iterated to the named level's own fixed point (2 cos Omega its eigenvalue), the eigensolver started from the one seeded vector at the one tolerance; the level's phi = p chi / sqrt(cos U) (the 2p the triplet's combination with the largest dipole along x), normalised to 1 at its largest with its sign positive at the centre for an s level and along +x for the p; beside it every kept level's Omega and kind."""
    shape = well.shape
    flat = well.ravel()
    grids = [
        g.astype(np.float64).ravel()
        for g in np.meshgrid(*(np.arange(e) - e // 2 for e in shape), indexing="ij")
    ]
    scale = (1 / np.cos(flat) ** (1 / 2)) * (pace.ravel() / pace.max())
    start = np.random.default_rng(START_SEED).standard_normal(flat.size)
    omega = omega_0 - START_BELOW
    for _ in range(ITERATIONS):
        values, vectors = eigsh(
            operator(reaches, own, pace, well, omega, periodic),
            k=SOLVED,
            which="LA",
            v0=start,
            tol=TOLERANCE,
        )
        order = np.argsort(-values)[:LEVELS]  # the top levels kept, the solver's cut beyond them
        values, vectors = values[order], vectors[:, order] * scale[:, None]
        kinds = [kind_of(vectors[:, j], grids) for j in range(LEVELS)]
        index = level_index(kinds, level)
        found = float(np.arccos(values[index] / 2))
        if abs(found - omega) < TOLERANCE:
            omega = found
            break
        omega = found
    if KINDS[level][0] == "p":
        triplet = [vectors[:, j] for j in (index, index + 1, index + 2)]
        weights = [float((v * grids[0]).sum()) for v in triplet]
        phi = sum(w * v for w, v in zip(weights, triplet, strict=True))
        phi = phi * np.sign(float((phi * grids[0]).sum()))
    else:
        phi = vectors[:, index]
        phi = phi * np.sign(phi[int(np.argmax(np.abs(phi)))])
    phi = phi / np.abs(phi).max()
    table = [
        {
            "level": j,
            "kind": kinds[j],
            "Omega": float(np.arccos(values[j] / 2)),
            "binding_per_interval": omega_0 - float(np.arccos(values[j] / 2)),
        }
        for j in range(LEVELS)
    ]
    return phi, omega, table


def level_names(text: str) -> str:
    """The levels `--level` names, one of the kinds table's or several joined by '+' (the lay their sum, each once); refused by name otherwise."""
    names = text.split("+")
    if not names or len(set(names)) != len(names) or any(name not in KINDS for name in names):
        raise argparse.ArgumentTypeError(
            f"--level takes one of {list(KINDS)} or several of them joined by '+', each once, got {text!r}"
        )
    return text


def standing(
    board: Lattice,
    index: int,
    well: np.ndarray,
    action: int,
    periodic: tuple[bool, bool, bool],
    level: str,
    shares: tuple[int, ...] = (),
    seed: int = 0,
) -> tuple[dict[str, np.ndarray], dict[str, Any]]:
    """The standing lay of the named level, or of several levels joined by '+' (the design verdict of 2026-10-19, section 5, the line: the step is linear, so the sum of standing solutions is a solution; the lay is the sum of the named levels' lays, each level at its own Omega in the before term and the common well's angle on the now term, each at 1 / n of the quantum, A_k = sqrt(T / (2 n SUM phi_k^2 sin(Omega_k + U_i))), the four arrays summed before the rounding), from the well and the engine's own rule integers at every Node (the recipes' steps 2 to 4 in the generic form, the engine's phase convention) and the tool's readings beside it, the rule's integers over the wall among them: for one level its Omega, its binding, its amplitude A and its phi along the axis as before; for a sum the same per level by the level's name, and the beats between the levels (Omega of the later named less the earlier per interval, the period 2 pi over it, the levels' overlap SUM phi_k phi_l and their dipole overlap SUM x phi_k phi_l per axis, the line's own numbers)."""
    names = level.split("+")
    num, den = board.families[index].pair
    omega_0 = float(np.arccos(num / den))
    reaches, own, pace = rule_arrays(board, index)
    shape = well.shape
    centre = tuple(e // 2 for e in shape)
    count = len(names)
    parts = shares or (1,) * count  # the levels' shares of the quantum, equal where none are given
    if len(parts) != count or min(parts) < 1:
        raise ValueError(f"--shares names one share from 1 per level of {level!r}, got {list(parts)}")
    sums = {key: np.zeros(shape, dtype=np.float64) for key in ("now", "im_now", "before", "im_before")}
    laid: list[dict[str, Any]] = []
    cubes: list[np.ndarray] = []
    for name, part in zip(names, parts, strict=True):
        phi, omega, table = eigenvectors(reaches, own, pace, well, omega_0, periodic, name)
        cube = phi.reshape(shape)
        total = float((cube**2 * np.sin(omega + well)).sum())
        amplitude = (action * part / (2 * sum(parts) * total)) ** (1 / 2)
        half = (
            well / 2
        )  # the centred count: the Link's phase at the step centred at the lay is half the Node's angle
        sums["now"] += amplitude * cube * np.cos(half)
        sums["im_now"] += -amplitude * cube * np.sin(half)
        sums["before"] += amplitude * cube * np.cos(omega + half)
        sums["im_before"] += amplitude * cube * np.sin(omega + half)
        cubes.append(cube)
        laid.append(
            {
                "level": name,
                "Omega": omega,
                "binding_per_interval": omega_0 - omega,
                "A": amplitude,
                "phi_along_axis": [float(v) for v in cube[centre[0] :, centre[1], centre[2]]],
                "levels": table,
            }
        )
    dither = np.random.default_rng(seed) if seed else None  # the rounding seed: within the lay's grain
    lay = {
        key: np.rint(value + (dither.random(shape) - 1 / 2 if dither else 0)).astype(np.int64)
        for key, value in sums.items()
    }
    grids = np.meshgrid(*(np.arange(e) - c for e, c in zip(shape, centre, strict=True)), indexing="ij")
    beats = [
        {
            "levels": f"{laid[k]['level']}+{laid[m]['level']}",
            "per_interval": laid[m]["Omega"] - laid[k]["Omega"],
            "period_intervals": 2 * float(np.pi) / abs(laid[m]["Omega"] - laid[k]["Omega"]),
            "overlap": float((cubes[k] * cubes[m]).sum()),
            "dipole_overlap_along_axes": [float((cubes[k] * cubes[m] * g).sum()) for g in grids],
        }
        for k in range(count)
        for m in range(k + 1, count)
    ]
    one = count == 1
    readings: dict[str, Any] = {
        "lay": "standing",
        "level": level,
        "Omega": laid[0]["Omega"] if one else {row["level"]: row["Omega"] for row in laid},
        "omega_0": omega_0,
        "binding_per_interval": laid[0]["binding_per_interval"]
        if one
        else {row["level"]: row["binding_per_interval"] for row in laid},
        "A": laid[0]["A"] if one else {row["level"]: row["A"] for row in laid},
        "phi_along_axis": laid[0]["phi_along_axis"]
        if one
        else {row["level"]: row["phi_along_axis"] for row in laid},
        "levels": laid[0]["levels"] if one else {row["level"]: row["levels"] for row in laid},
        "levels_note": "every Omega of the table is read with the named level's sin Omega in the operator's diagonal; another level at its own sin Omega moves by that term's change, the order of the binding",
        "rule_over_wall": {
            "reaches": [[float(r.min()), float(r.max())] for r in reaches],
            "own_weight": [float(own.min()), float(own.max())],
            "paces": [float(pace.min()), float(pace.max())],
            "note": "R_ij / w per Port, S_i / w and the Node's pace p_i from the engine's own read and rule at the start; the plain rule at Gamma reads num / (3 den) on every Link and 0 at the Node",
        },
        "convention": "now = A phi cos(U / 2), im_now = -A phi sin(U / 2), before = A phi cos(Omega + U / 2), im_before = A phi sin(Omega + U / 2): the centred count (the owner's decision of 2026-10-23), the step centred at the lay carrying half the Node's angle on its Links; to that day now = A phi cos U, im_now = -A phi sin U, before = A phi cos Omega, im_before = A phi sin Omega",
    }
    if not one:
        readings["sum"] = (
            "the lay is the sum of the named levels' lays, each level at its own Omega in the before term and the "
            "common well's angle on the now term, each at its share s_k of the quantum (--shares, 1 / n where none "
            "are given), A_k = sqrt(s_k T / (2 SUM phi_k^2 sin(Omega_k + U_i))), the four arrays summed before the "
            "rounding"
        )
        readings["shares"] = [part / sum(parts) for part in parts]
        readings["beats"] = beats
    readings["seed"] = seed  # the rounding seed of the lay, 0 the plain rounding
    return lay, readings


def gaussian(
    shape: tuple[int, ...], pair: tuple[int, int], action: int, sigma: float
) -> tuple[dict[str, np.ndarray], dict[str, Any]]:
    """The free lump, the builder's probe's lay that does not stand: a Gaussian of width sigma at the free rotation, with the floor divisions of that lay."""
    num, den = pair
    sine = paces.sine_den(num, den)
    axes = [np.arange(extent) - extent // 2 for extent in shape]
    g = np.exp(
        -(axes[0][:, None, None] ** 2 + axes[1][None, :, None] ** 2 + axes[2][None, None, :] ** 2)
        / (2 * sigma * sigma)
    )
    scale = (action * den / (2 * sine * float((g * g).sum()))) ** (1 / 2)
    now = np.rint(g * scale).astype(np.int64)
    lay = {
        "now": now,
        "before": now * num // den,
        "im_now": np.zeros_like(now),
        "im_before": now * sine // den,
    }
    return lay, {
        "lay": "gaussian",
        "sigma": sigma,
        "omega_0": float(np.arccos(num / den)),
        "scale": scale,
    }


def profile(lay: dict[str, np.ndarray], centre: tuple[int, int, int]) -> dict[str, Any]:
    """The lay's radial profile about the centre: the share of Q = |z|^2 within each radius, Q itself, the peak level and its Node, the lay's dipole SUM (x_i - c) q_i / Q per axis in Nodes (a line's amplitude at the lay, 0 for a level), the Wronskian SUM now x im_before - im_now x before."""
    shape = lay["now"].shape
    grids = np.meshgrid(*(np.arange(e) - c for e, c in zip(shape, centre, strict=True)), indexing="ij")
    radius = sum(g.astype(float) ** 2 for g in grids) ** (1 / 2)
    q = lay["now"].astype(float) ** 2 + lay["im_now"].astype(float) ** 2
    total = float(q.sum())
    peak = np.unravel_index(int(np.argmax(q)), shape)
    radii = [r for r in RADII if r <= shape[0] // 2]
    return {
        "radii": radii,
        "shares": [float(q[radius <= r].sum()) / total for r in radii],
        "Q": total,
        "peak_level": float(q[peak] ** (1 / 2)),
        "peak_node": [int(v) for v in peak],
        "size_along_axis": [
            float(q[centre[0] + d, centre[1], centre[2]] ** (1 / 2))
            for d in range(0, shape[0] // 2 + 1, 2)
        ],
        "node_plane_share": float(q[centre[0], :, :].sum()) / total,
        "dipole_nodes": [float((q * g).sum()) / total for g in grids],
        "wronskian": float(
            (
                lay["now"].astype(float) * lay["im_before"].astype(float)
                - lay["im_now"].astype(float) * lay["before"].astype(float)
            ).sum()
        ),
    }


def main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> None:
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.splitlines()[0])
    parser.add_argument(
        "--input", type=Path, required=True, help="the world file; the mode file is written beside it"
    )
    parser.add_argument("--record", required=True, help="the family of the record laid standing")
    parser.add_argument(
        "--source", required=True, help="the family of the one-Node sources laid as pixel records"
    )
    parser.add_argument("--sense", type=int, required=True, choices=(-1, 1), help="the sources' sense")
    parser.add_argument(
        "--lay", default="standing", choices=("standing", "gaussian"), help="the record's lay"
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--level",
        default="1s",
        type=level_names,
        help="the level laid standing, or several joined by '+' and summed, e.g. 1s+2p (--lay standing)",
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--sigma", type=float, default=SIGMA, help="the Gaussian's width in Nodes (--lay gaussian)"
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--shares",
        type=lambda text: tuple(int(v) for v in text.split(",")),
        default=(),
        help="the levels' shares of the quantum in the order --level names them, integers from 1 over their sum, e.g. 1,9 (equal where absent)",
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--seed",
        type=int,
        default=0,
        help="the lay's rounding seed: the levels dithered within half a unit before their rounding, so that the lay differs by at most one unit per Node (0, the plain rounding)",
    )
    args = parser.parse_args(argv)
    path: Path = args.input
    world = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    shape = tuple(int(v) for v in world["shape"])
    mode_path = path.with_suffix(".mode.json")
    packets = (
        json.loads(mode_path.read_text(encoding="utf-8")).get("packets", [])
        if mode_path.exists()
        else []
    )  # the packets' entries the generator wrote (tools/pixel_mode.py), carried through: the standing lay is the bodies'
    universe = universe_of_world(world)
    families = universe_of(universe)[1]
    action, gamma = int(universe["integers"]["quantum_action"]), int(universe["integers"]["node_clock"])
    # (1) the well's reading pass: the sources laid, the record at 0, the holder's rows the engine's own start writes
    entries = entries_of(world, families, args.record, args.source, args.sense, zero_lay(shape))
    mode_path.write_text(json.dumps(mode_document(world, entries, packets)) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
    h, index, holder, weight, board = well_of(path, args.record)
    family = families[index]
    well = well_angles(
        board, index, gamma
    )  # the Node's angle per interval from the engine's own rounded count
    periodic = (
        str(world["boundary"]["x"]) == "periodic",
        str(world["boundary"]["y"]) == "periodic",
        str(world["boundary"]["z"]) == "periodic",
    )
    # (2) to (4) the lay
    if args.lay == "standing":
        lay, readings = standing(
            board, index, well, action, periodic, args.level, args.shares, args.seed
        )
    else:
        lay, readings = gaussian(shape, family.pair, action, args.sigma)
    entries = entries_of(world, families, args.record, args.source, args.sense, lay)
    mode_path.write_text(json.dumps(mode_document(world, entries, packets)) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
    load_world(path)  # the loader admits the mode file beside the world
    centre = tuple(e // 2 for e in shape)
    readings.update(
        label=LABEL,
        world=path.name,
        record=args.record,
        source=args.source,
        holder=families[holder].name,
        k_r=weight,
        node_clock=gamma,
        quantum_action=action,
        well_along_axis=[int(v) for v in h[centre[0] :, centre[1], centre[2]]],
        well_centre=float(well[centre]),
        profile=profile(lay, (centre[0], centre[1], centre[2])),
    )
    path.with_suffix(".standing.json").write_text(
        json.dumps(readings, indent=1) + "\n", encoding="utf-8"
    )
    summary: dict[str, Any] = {
        k: readings[k]
        for k in ("world", "lay", "level", "record", "Omega", "omega_0", "binding_per_interval", "A")
        if k in readings
    }
    summary.update(
        peak=readings["profile"]["peak_level"],
        shares=[round(v, 3) for v in readings["profile"]["shares"]],
        mode=str(mode_path),
    )
    print(json.dumps(summary))


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
